@model string
@*
    Lanes of code scrolling slowly and endlessly, like a looping animated background
    (ADR-0008). The variant decides where they live: "hero" is the stronger layer inside
    the hero, "page" is a fainter layer fixed behind the whole page so the motion
    continues as the visitor scrolls. Both use the same lanes, so the background reads as
    one continuous surface from the top of the page to the bottom.

    Lanes have no positions of their own: the stylesheet lays them out as equal-width grid
    columns across the full width, so two lanes can never overlap. Each lane's code is
    rendered twice in a row and the stylesheet scrolls exactly half its height, so the loop
    has no visible jump.

    Purely decorative: hidden from assistive technology, no pointer events, and the
    stylesheet stops the motion for visitors who prefer reduced motion.
*@
@using Portfolio.Web.Content
<div class="code-streams code-streams--@Model" aria-hidden="true">
    @foreach (var stream in BackdropCode.Streams)
    {
        <div class="code-stream" style="--dur:@(stream.Seconds)s;--dir:@(stream.Reverse ? "reverse" : "normal")"><pre>@stream.Code
@stream.Code</pre></div>
    }
</div>
